vel . In some areas of the State , the ever - increasing need for land on which to build express highways and airports is already causing severe problems for the public agencies responsible for providing these transportation facilities .\n\nFor its initial investigation into possible improved intercity rail service for New York State , the route between New York City and Binghamton was selected because the Southern Tier area has relatively less satisfactory alternate modes of travel to New York City and elsewhere . Pending the completion of Route 17 improvements , the Binghamton area is highly dependent on rail service , particularly so during periods of bad weather when roads are snow - covered and flying is limited .\n\nThe fastest rail service presently scheduled between New York City and Binghamton is four hours and twenty minutes for 192 miles . Preliminary investigation by this Office indicated that , for an initial phase operation using presently available equipment , it would be technically feasible to provide a limited stop service between these two points with a running time of about three - and - a - quarter hours . This would constitute a much more satisfactory travel time by today's standards of speed for other modes of transportation .\n\nThe results of this investigation were presented in July , 1963 ,... A committee was formed from this group to work with the Erie- Lackawanna Railroad to explore the possibilities of the plan . ", "full": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:66ectx3gi4ffi3gtbnxrxvlh/bafkreifedv6mwppf7yqz3ngwik45krj7wpq55d35xz6gq3bn4xpapof6tu", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:66ectx3gi4ffi3gtbnxrxvlh/bafkreifedv6mwppf7yqz3ngwik45krj7wpq55d35xz6gq3bn4xpapof6tu"}]}, {"at": "2026-07-18T16:43:14.676Z", "name": "Nolan Hicks", "text": "babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=ie...", "quote": null, "handle": "ndhapple.bsky.social"}, {"at": "2026-07-18T17:12:22.582Z", "name": "Nolan Hicks", "text": "Using the PJ to reactivate the old Wallkill Valley RR ROW to get service to New Paltz and Kingston would also do numbers, IMO. \n\nPut a New Paltz-Kingston service on top of a regular commuter line on top of Binghamton train and all of a sudden you've got a WofH artery worth spending money on.", "quote": null, "handle": "ndhapple.bsky.social", "images": [{"alt": "A map of the old Walkill Valley ROW in blue (the actual ROW is a bit twistier but it basically followed the blue path. Annoying, Railmap won't show the Walkill ROW on anything but the tightest zoom level, which makes it impossible to illustrate the route.) ", "full": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:66ectx3gi4ffi3gtbnxrxvlh/bafkreiapazo7zszxevcs4fcbzveqnhrr3xwl7vveluatu6bscuhjb7h55m", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:66ectx3gi4ffi3gtbnxrxvlh/bafkreiapazo7zszxevcs4fcbzveqnhrr3xwl7vveluatu6bscuhjb7h55m"}]}, {"at": "2026-07-18T17:13:20.475Z", "name": "Nolan Hicks", "text": "The college kids and Kingston weekenders alone would pack the trains", "quote": null, "handle": "ndhapple.bsky.social"}]}, "favicon_url" : "https://web-cdn.bsky.app/static/favicon-32x32.png", "image_url" : null, "site_name" : "Bluesky Social", "inserted_at" : "2026-07-31T22:13:36", "dead_at" : null, "comment_count" : 0, "save_count" : 0, "chat_count" : 0}, {"id" : 42, "url" : "https://bsky.app/profile/tmsparks.bsky.social/post/3mpukosjnwk2t", "title" : "Post by @tmsparks.bsky.social — Bluesky", "description" : null, "tags" : ["bluesky","fireworks","nyc","bridges","4th-of-july"], "quotes" : [], "thread" : {"posts": [{"at": "2026-07-05T02:46:18.458Z", "name": "Erowid Smoothie", "text": "Now that I have better service the fireworks streaming off the bottom of the Brooklyn bridge were really fuckin cool:", "quote": {"name": "Erowid Smoothie", "text": "Standing on the FDR Drive, watchin some fireworks w/ @bobbby.online and @eastcoastemo.bsky.social", "handle": "tmsparks.bsky.social", "images": [{"a